      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "# Nexus Optic-7 Quick-Start Guide\n\n## Introduction\nThe Nexus Optic-7 is a state-of-the-art Lidar-based proximity sensor designed for versatile applications. This guide provides essential information to ensure safe and efficient operation.\n\n## Specifications\n- **Model:** Nexus Optic-7 (Lidar-based proximity sensor)\n- **Operating Voltage:** 5V - 12V DC\n- **Connection:** 4-pin waterproof connector (Red: VCC, Black: GND, Yellow: Signal, Green: Sync)\n- **Mounting:** M3 screw holes, max torque 0.5Nm\n- **Calibration:** Requires 30s warm-up; press Sync button once for auto-calibration\n- **Safety:** Do not look directly into lens during operation; avoid submersion above 2m.\n- **Range:** 0.1m to 40m\n\n## Installation\n1. Mount the sensor using the M3 screw holes, ensuring the max torque of 0.5Nm is not exceeded.\n2. Connect the 4-pin waterproof connector: Red to VCC, Black to GND, Yellow to Signal, and Green to Sync.\n3. Power the sensor within the operating voltage",
